WEBVTT

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.456
And I was thinking about this,
what to talk about at TED.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.656
When I talked to the kind rep from TED,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.376
and I said, "Listen, you know,
what should I talk about?"

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.776
He said, "Don't worry about it.
Just be profound."

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.096
(Laughter)

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.856
And I took enormous comfort in that.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.496
So thank you, if you're here.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.336
I was trying to think,
what do I talk about? Good question.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.616
Why do I do so much
stuff that involves mystery?

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.496
And I started trying to figure it out.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.256
And I started thinking
about why do I do any of what I do,

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.376
and I started thinking
about my grandfather.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.176
I loved my grandfather.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.296
Harry Kelvin was his name,
my mother's father.